                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f5ae832d-c857-497e-875b-f0a88b489a6d",
                        "source_entry_id": "2dbe7d87-4ef9-39c7-a9c4-7c9e9cd1da93",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c8df5f9-7922-336e-b1ba-a0c91dbba528",
                        "target_lang_word": "acropolis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "acropolis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f54a7786-393a-3208-ae6d-22f00ee84b1e",
                                        "entry_id": "9f3de74c-cd0c-31fc-814f-ce517ef568ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A promontory (usually fortified with a citadel) forming the hub of many Grecian cities, and around which many were built for defensive purposes before and during the classical period; compare Acropolis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc76719a-8ae4-4ca8-97a9-471373fa8a2a",
                                                "sense_id": "f54a7786-393a-3208-ae6d-22f00ee84b1e",
                                                "text": "The Etruscans, then, appear in general as an industrious people ( φιλότεχνον ἔθνος), of a bold and lofty spirit of enterprise, which was greatly favoured by their priestly aristocratic constitution. Massive walls, mostly of irregular blocks, surround their cities (not merely their acropoleis); the art of protecting the country from inundations by the construction of canals, and outlets from lakes, was very zealously practised by them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "267574cb-f519-4735-9dd5-57b0c6b2d080",
                        "source_entry_id": "2dbe7d87-4ef9-39c7-a9c4-7c9e9cd1da93",
                        "source_sense_id": "2c8df5f9-7922-336e-b1ba-a0c91dbba528",
                        "target_lang_word": "acropole",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "acropole",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                        "entry_id": "ce13f1a6-20ea-3e33-a20b-4bfcaf37bf76",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ville haute, partie de la ville située sur une éminence fortifiée par la nature et par l’art et contenant le principal temple de la cité."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9deff668-f6e1-4365-9f7d-5b9d225ae68b",
                                                "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                                "text": "Une acropole était à la fois une citadelle et un sanctuaire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f311650e-2001-42f0-8616-ee336f4d39a2",
                                                "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                                "text": "La plus célèbre de toutes les acropoles est celle d’Athènes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "691b7ab4-0707-47f7-8aa4-c31d307eba4e",
                                                "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                                "text": "L’acropole de Corinthe portait le nom particulier d’Acrocorinthe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3de8aec-4f41-4a39-8643-69a692090530",
                                                "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                                "text": "Les premiers sondages avaient révélé qu'une partie des constructions de l'acropole avaient été détruites par le feu."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b25cc633-89ba-4411-972a-8f4418a737e2",
                                                "sense_id": "814b9d78-1576-3eba-a5d0-dbe498573845",
                                                "text": "Mieux qu'Athenes, le pont d'un bateau en route vers les Amériques offre à l'homme moderne une acropole pour sa prière."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
